AB  - In this study, a novel virus isolated from Nigrospora oryzae, tentatively named 'Nigrospora oryzae mycovirus 1' (NoMyV1), was identified. NoMyV1 has a non-segmented dsRNA genome that is 2891 bp in length and contains two non-overlapping open reading frames (ORF1 and 2). ORF1 encodes a protein with sequence similarity to the putative capsid proteins or hypothetical proteins of other unclassified viruses, while ORF2 encodes an RNA-dependent RNA polymerase (RdRp). Sequence comparisons showed that NoMyV1 was most similar to Penicillium janczewskii Beauveria bassiana-like virus 1 (PjBblV1), with 76.12% amino acid sequence identity in the RdRp. In a phylogenetic analysis based on RdRp sequences, NoMyV1 was found to cluster with several other unclassified viruses for which a new genus, 'Unirnavirus', which is distinct from the family Partitiviridae, has been proposed. Thus, we conclude that NoMyV1 is a novel member of the proposed genus 'Unirnavirus'.
